            "icon": "dentistry",
            "filled_icon": true,
            "collapse_icon": "carret",
            "display_top_border": true,
            "open": false,
            "content": "<p>Daily removal clears plaque before it hardens into tartar. Here's what you'll typically see in your dog:</p><p><strong>Week 1 </strong>— bad breath noticeably improves, usually the first change owners spot.</p><p><strong>Week 2</strong>— teeth start to look cleaner as surface plaque and staining lighten, and the gumline looks calmer and less red.</p><p><strong>Week 3</strong>— visibly cleaner teeth, consistently fresh breath, and no new buildup forming.</p><p>Every wipe comes away coated in the plaque and bacteria you just removed — visible proof it's lifting buildup off the tooth, not smearing it around like a smooth wipe.</p>",
